description:
Open-source contribution opportunity. Repository: yjiao4903-lang/cross-asset. Labels: enhancement, help wanted. ## WEB-CONTROL refreshed scope — 2026-09-13

### Goal

Establish the first provider-neutral real-data Marco → Cross E2E and make the daily workbench freshness/calendar path actually reachable without reviving the retired automated Wind dependency.

Current evidence from ARCH-REDTEAM #107 shows the main daily path is structurally DATA_BLOCKED because `config/series_calendars.yml` is empty and calendars remain unverified. This Issue now owns the calendar/evidence/E2E integration surface; real source bytes remain owned by #93/#104.

### Authoritative dependencies

- #93: user-supplied/manual professional-source market/FX/DXY data intake and research admission.
- #104: official-source CN_M1/CN_M2/CN_DR007 verification.
- #108: completed external evidence/export-spec research for market/FX/DXY/GOLD/COPPER; research evidence only, not admission.
- #20/#106: daily/shadow WorkbenchRun and lineage implementation; do not duplicate it here.
- #81: remains blocked until a fresh combined readiness rebuild is genuinely READY.

Automated Wind/WindPy acquisition is retired. Professional terminals may be used only as user manual-export sources under #93.

## Scope A — calendar evidence and bindings

For every formal required daily market/FX series used by the daily path, establish the exact calendar/timezone/session/freshness semantics needed by `engines/freshness.py` and populate the smallest provider-neutral configuration required to make those checks meaningful.

At minimum cover the six market sleeves and accounting FX inputs when admitted:
- `CN_EQ_LARGE`
- `HK_EQ`
- `US_EQ`
- `CN_BOND_10Y`
- `GOLD`
- `COPPER`
- USD/CNY accounting FX
- HKD/CNY accounting FX

Requirements:
- verified calendar identity;
- timezone;
- normal close/settle or publication convention;
- holidays / early-close behavior where materially relevant;
- CN_INTERBANK make-up working days where applicable;
- explicit freshness lag budget;
- no generic weekend substitution for China interbank semantics;
- no guessed calendar mappings.

If evidence is insufficient, remain `UNVERIFIED / DATA_BLOCKED`.

## Scope B — series catalog / freshness metadata integration

ARCH-REDTEAM #107 found `series_catalog` has no production population path, making stale-after-hours checks/data-health partially dead in a real database. Implement or reuse the smallest idempotent loader from the accepted config/source semantics into the existing catalog contract.

No parallel catalog or readiness framework. No silent defaults.

Regression should prove:
- configured series receives the expected freshness metadata;
- missing mapping remains blocked;
- unverified calendar remains blocked;
- stale series is distinguishable from missing/unknown;
- a healthy formally consumable series can pass when all evidence is present.

## Scope C — first real provider-neutral E2E

Once #93/#104 have supplied/admitted enough real inputs, run the existing formal path only:

`immutable evidence -> semantic validation -> registry/admission -> sanctioned query -> freshness/calendar -> market/macro/style -> score -> allocation -> WorkbenchRun/report`

The E2E artifact must record:
- source_mode;
- run_id;
- data_cutoff;
- model/config identity;
- source evidence identities;
- coverage/freshness status;
- warnings/blockers;
- ACTIVE/FROZEN/DATA_BLOCKED truthfully.

Fixture/simulated evidence remains separate and cannot satisfy this target.

## Scope D — daily/research object consistency

Do not force fake parity. Either prove daily and research paths consume the same accepted model/input semantics, or explicitly disclose where they remain incomparable. Valuation/carry/structure remain unavailable until auditable inputs exist; do not zero-fill or tune proxies.

## Acceptance

- provider-neutral calendar bindings are evidence-backed and usable by the freshness engine;
- `series_catalog`/freshness metadata is no longer test-only/dead in real operation;
- missing/unverified/stale semantics remain fail-closed;
- when real admitted data exists, one Marco→Cross run can be reproduced from manifest/evidence without future leakage;
- no automated Wind dependency is reintroduced;
- no proxy/default/zero-fill; `UNKNOWN != ZERO`, `MISSING != ZERO`.

## Boundaries

- no strategic/tactical weight change;
- no schema migration unless separately authorized;
- no #20 lineage reimplementation;
- no #104 source duplication;
- no #81 activation/holdout release;
- no claim that CI/fixture equals real-data readiness.

Final implementation should be dispatched only when dependencies/evidence are ready; until then this Issue is the authoritative P1 calendar/E2E integration target.
